#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264499 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "045722b6-b558-522b-86e1-322c64e2848f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Limit of a Rational Function with a Radical in the Denominator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9522321-d07c-5a20-b5a9-f2ebff52419f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264501} {:answer/id #uuid "1b2dbd48-6baf-5e15-bbfb-b49df51606ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{7}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264502} {:answer/id #uuid "934ab8eb-0b43-5dbc-8b63-94acc00d4e00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264503} {:answer/id #uuid "136c30fa-9044-52a8-8a49-837a101f76ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264504} {:answer/id #uuid "f330557c-b754-5f71-a0c9-29586f4eec50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264505}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b2dbd48-6baf-5e15-bbfb-b49df51606ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{7}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264502} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdaf86b8-fe13-5914-bc47-1912531cc01e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264500}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4657fda3-adb3-52a6-b9ad-8af5d9861fcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-101288" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{3x+1}-\\sqrt{7}}=$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=2$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{3x+1}-\\sqrt{7}} & =\\frac{2-2}{\\sqrt{3(2)+1}-\\sqrt{7}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-2}{\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{7}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{3x+1}-\\sqrt{7}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(x-2)(\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7})}{(\\sqrt{3x+1}-\\sqrt{7})(\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(x-2)(\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7})}{(\\sqrt{3x+1})^{2}-(\\sqrt{7})^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(x-2)(\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7})}{3x+1-7} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(x-2)(\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7})}{3x-6} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(x-2)(\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7})}{3(x-2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3(2)+1}+\\sqrt{7}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{7}+\\sqrt{7}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{7}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264545 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a441c8ef-b5b3-5438-97b9-53e4eb7b2d75" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Limit of a Rational Function with a Radical in the Numerator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c6042be-68e6-5614-b52d-6187961da820" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264547} {:answer/id #uuid "c39a0edb-c621-53b4-845d-43c733153aa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264548} {:answer/id #uuid "d5a9454a-fd37-5f0a-94d4-516aff72fd65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264549} {:answer/id #uuid "659ab017-b94c-5292-b78f-13b403f41670" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264550} {:answer/id #uuid "23eb41e1-df86-5d23-b317-2c9449eb29ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5a9454a-fd37-5f0a-94d4-516aff72fd65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264549} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3bffd14-44d5-5a70-ab62-289469c303c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264546}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c2192068-6d96-59a7-8da5-820238c32032" :question/math-academy-id "q-46838" :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2x-10\\sqrt{x}}{x-25}.$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2x-10\\sqrt{x}}{x-25} & =\\frac{50-10\\sqrt{25}}{25-25}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2x-10\\sqrt{x}}{x-25} & ={lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2(x-5\\sqrt{x})}{x-25} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2(x-5\\sqrt{x})(x+5\\sqrt{x})}{(x-25)(x+5\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2({x}^{2}-{(5\\sqrt{x})}^{2})}{(x-25)(x+5\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2({x}^{2}-25x)}{(x-25)(x+5\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2x(x-25)}{(x-25)(x+5\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2x}{x+5\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(25)}{25+5\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
